{"chunk_id":"ace7d6","wall_time_seconds":0.4363376,"exit_code":0,"original_token_count":10458,"output":"{"Content":"# Nordljud 2.0 — Software Construction Project Charter\r\n\r\n**Course:** Software Construction (SWCON2627), Åbo Akademi University  \r\n**Project Type:** Comparative, AI-Assisted Software Construction Experience Report  \r\n**Developer:** One student, working with AI-assisted development tools  \r\n**Target:** Address all sections of the 35-point project report rubric.  \r\n**Charter approval:** Student approved PC-001 in the ChatGPT conversation on 28 October 2026. Document archived with AI drafting assistance.\r\n\r\n## 1. Project Goal\r\n\r\nI want to develop a Swedish language learning web application called Nordljud and compare two different AI-assisted software development approaches: Vibe Coding and Specification-Driven Development (SDD) using GitHub Spec Kit.\r\n\r\nMy objective is not only to build working software but also to understand how the development methods differ in requirements handling, implementation, testing, debugging and the quality of the resulting software.\r\n\r\n## 2. Product Scope\r\n\r\nNordljud will support four Swedish learning levels: A2, B1, B2 and C1.\r\n\r\nThe agreed classroom MVP will include level-specific learning missions, Swedish–English vocabulary exploration using the shared teaching dataset, verb forms, translation assistance, pronunciation, interactive exercises, favorites, user authentication and saved learning progress.\r\n\r\nThe existing dataset contains 456 meaning records per level and 455 distinct written verbs, including two separate meanings of *sticka*.\r\n\r\nThe application should also support guest usage, responsive design and separation of authenticated users\u0027 saved data.\r\n\r\n## 3. Development Methods\r\n\r\n**Condition A — Vibe Coding:** I will communicate my requirements in natural language, review each prompt before execution, observe what the AI produces, test the results and provide further instructions when changes are necessary. The development will remain iterative rather than being driven by a complete upfront technical specification.\r\n\r\n**Condition B — Specification-Driven Development:** I will use the official GitHub Spec Kit workflow and a supported coding agent to establish project principles, define and clarify requirements, produce plans and tasks, implement the software and verify convergence.\r\n\r\nBoth conditions will use the same product scope, source dataset, technology constraints and independent evaluation criteria. Their application code will be developed separately.\r\n\r\n## 4. Technology\r\n\r\nThe proposed common stack is TypeScript, React, Next.js, Supabase, GitHub and Vercel. Dependency versions and external configuration will be recorded and controlled before implementation.\r\n\r\n## 5. Evaluation and Evidence\r\n\r\nI will preserve the real prompts, important AI outputs, Git commits, specifications, test cases, failures, corrections, screenshots and verification results.\r\n\r\nBoth implementations will be assessed using common acceptance scenarios and automated checks. Each important requirement will have an identifiable verification result: PASS, FAIL, BLOCKED or NOT TESTED.\r\n\r\n## 6. Academic Integrity and Limitations\r\n\r\nThe earlier Nordljud repository will remain unchanged as a pilot project. This second iteration will be documented as an informed redevelopment, not an independent first-time experiment.\r\n\r\nI will distinguish my own instructions from AI-assisted prompt drafting and AI-generated code. I will also report known limitations, including prior experience, development-order effects and unavailable measurements, without inventing evidence.\r\n\r\n## 7. Final Deliverables\r\n\r\nThe final submission will include two independently implemented applications, their Git histories, authentic prompt and specification records, testing evidence, comparative analysis, reflections, a proposed reusable SDD workflow and an experience report following the university\u0027s official template.\r\n","Path":"docs/PROJECT_CHARTER_PC-001.md"}
{"Content":"# Nordljud 2.0 — shared classroom product brief (A and B)\r\n\r\n**Status:** Fixed common goal approved as part of PC-001; this is deliberately NOT a complete SRS and NOT a coding prompt.\r\n\r\nA responsive **Swedish-through-English** learning web app for A2, B1, B2 and C1. One representative mission per level, each with a source-backed Swedish example, English assistance, browser Swedish speech (`sv-SE`) with graceful fallback, a comprehension check, a verb-form check, correct/incorrect feedback and saved learning status.\r\n\r\nExplore the **entire source lexicon** by level. Each level has 456 *meaning/sense* records and 455 different spellings: `sticka` is represented by two independent senses. Show the supplied five verb forms where available; do not invent missing forms or example sentences. Preserve the selected semantic sense when switching level and allow per-sense favorites.\r\n\r\nGuest use should work without sign-in; authentication by email/password and Google, account-specific favorites and progress restored after reload/sign-in, and a clear sign-out flow are expected in the full MVP. Do not assume provider credentials exist or misrepresent untested auth as working. Privacy must rely on appropriate server-side access controls such as Supabase RLS, not only UI hiding.\r\n\r\n**Common stack:** Next.js, React, TypeScript, Supabase, GitHub, Vercel, browser speech synthesis. Fix and report tested exact tool/dependency versions when development begins; no service-role credentials in client code or Git. Separate deployments and method-specific storage so one experimental condition does not erase another\u0027s progress.\r\n\r\n**Not in scope:** Payments, AI chat tutor, speech recognition or scoring, admin portal, social features, large curriculum creation, production-grade localization. Students should not be required to create hundreds of new lessons.\r\n\r\n**Experiment boundary:** Both methods start with the same data, these goals, and the same independent test obligations. Condition A develops through ordinary conversational prompts with student approval rather than receiving a fully engineered SRS; B creates its detailed specifications via Spec Kit before implementation. No old application source is supplied as new code.\r\n\r\nThe original inputs are historical and not Swedish-teacher-certified; provenance and permissions require review before publishing educational data publicly.\r\n","Path":"shared-content/PRODUCT_BRIEF.md"}
{"Content":"# Educational input provenance — Round 2\r\n\r\n**Source:** Owner\u0027s earlier private [Nordljud pilot](https://github.com/alikhalessi/nordljud-software-construction), branch `baseline-v1`, folder `shared-content/`. We deliberately import **data**, not prior application source. This is an informed redevelopment, not a blind independent experiment.\r\n\r\nThe files `verb-library/A2.json`, `B1.json`, `B2.json`, `C1.json` and `mission-seeds.json` were copied *byte-for-byte in Git blob identity* from the pilot, and their blob SHAs match. The corresponding GitHub source folder predates the prior A/B/C implementation.\r\n\r\n| Level | Sense records | Source Git blob SHA |\r\n|---|---:|---|\r\n| A2 | 456 | `b0064f93419503fe4ff967303490bb31284a3959` |\r\n| B1 | 456 | `b2ea9af945b72eafc008df20e5cc23541a0c6d9a` |\r\n| B2 | 456 | `11d79a803d72c7172eda5f09894e4e514c434ec6` |\r\n| C1 | 456 | `7b9e7121faf5c45038d845e92eda4f76b886c9cb` |\r\n\r\nThere are 1,824 level-specific sense records, but **456 sense records / 455 unique written verb spellings per level**, not 456 unique spellings. The two records spelled `sticka` represent distinct meanings and must retain separate identities. The older pilot SOURCE_MANIFEST\u0027s phrase “456 base verbs” is imprecise; preserve the original historical text but correct that interpretation for Round 2.\r\n\r\n**Earlier upstream provenance:** The pilot reports recovery from the owner\u0027s earlier Swedish-learning materials (`Nordlyd_3B_Demo.html`, `Nordlyd_3B_1_Ready_To_Deploy.zip`, 8 October 2026), themselves describing educational material from previously provided Swedish-learning PDFs. Those primary PDFs and any distribution licenses have *not* been rechecked. Existing Swedish examples, translations and level grading are **not Swedish-teacher-validated**.\r\n\r\nBlank verb forms/examples were preserved; missing text must not be hallucinated. Mission seeds are existing metadata, not an implemented application.\r\n\r\n**Publication caveat:** Keep this academic repo private until underlying data rights and educational accuracy are reviewed. Do not publish elevated credentials, real user records or live authentication secrets.\r\n\r\nThis manifest supports reuse of common *inputs*. It does not permit copying old HTML/CSS/React/auth logic/tests into the new implementations.\r\n","Path":"shared-content/SOURCE_MANIFEST.md"}
{"Content":"# Common independent acceptance matrix — pre-implementation version 1\r\n\r\nThis checklist is shared external evaluation evidence, **not** an SDD-style master prompt to be imposed on Vibe. Run equivalent black-box procedures against both frozen condition builds. Log environment, case steps, expected vs actual, status (PASS/FAIL/BLOCKED/NOT TESTED), screenshot/run URL and tested commit. A passing source compilation does not establish user-facing acceptance.\r\n\r\n| ID | Acceptance scenario | Observable expected outcome | Evidence type |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| F01 | Four levels | A2, B1, B2 and C1 are selectable; distinct source-linked missions appear | Guest browser |\r\n| F02 | Source sentences | Swedish text and English translation correspond to frozen inputs; reveal/hide assistance works | Browser/data |\r\n| F03 | Speech | Request Swedish speech when available, otherwise show meaningful unavailable status | Browser/manual |\r\n| F04 | Two practice checks | Correct **and incorrect** answers produce appropriate feedback, no credit for incorrect | Browser |\r\n| F05 | Lexicon completeness | Search and load 456 sense records for each of four levels | Source/API/browser |\r\n| F06 | Same spelling, different senses | Two `sticka` senses can be selected independently and retain correct meaning | Browser |\r\n| F07 | Level switch | Selected *sense* is stable across A2→C1 change, with level-specific examples | Browser |\r\n| F08 | Guest work | A guest can study and retain appropriate browser-scoped local state after reload | Browser |\r\n| F09 | Email authentication | Account registration, invalid credentials, sign-in and sign-out behave correctly | Live/manual |\r\n| F10 | Google OAuth | Hosted sign-in returns to hosted origin and authenticates, not localhost | Live/manual |\r\n| F11 | Cloud persistence | Personal mission completion and favorites survive refresh, sign-out and re-login | Live/manual |\r\n| F12 | Account isolation | Two different users cannot read or overwrite each other\u0027s saved state | Live/manual/RLS |\r\n| F13 | Mobile + keyboard | Essential study navigation and login operate on narrow viewport and keyboard | Browser |\r\n| F14 | Secrets and failures | No elevated keys in code/client; failures display actionable messages | Code audit/browser |\r\n| F15 | Reproducibility | Dependencies, tested commits, expected source count, typecheck and build are recorded | CI/source |\r\n\r\n**Controls:** Same test data and expectations both methods; report missing external credentials honestly; keep evidence raw; record both identical and method-specific failures. Do not claim a security penetration test without actually performing one.\r\n\r\n**Bias disclosure:** This is a second informed iteration; the student\u0027s past experience with the two-sense `sticka` and OAuth issues can affect either method. That cannot be removed retrospectively and is not evidence of a causal superiority result.\r\n","Path":"evaluation/ACCEPTANCE_MATRIX.md"}
{"Content":"# Comparison protocol — approved baseline, before implementation\r\n\r\n## Research question\r\nIn a second, informed iteration of Nordljud, how do **iterative Vibe Coding** and **GitHub Spec Kit-supported Specification-Driven Development** differ in the clarity of requirements, development evidence, observed defects, quality-gate outcomes, and delivered user experience?\r\n\r\n## Conditions and scope\r\nA = natural student-approved prompts and feedback-driven increments; B = actual official Spec Kit agent workflow (constitution → specify/clarify → plan → tasks → implement → converge) with review checkpoints. No God Mode. Both start from the same shared baseline, frozen teaching data and common product goal. Different codebases. The historical prototype and pilot may inform the **student\u0027s understanding**; previous app code/tests must not be used as implementation templates for either method.\r\n\r\n## Controls\r\n- Same approved classroom scope and datasets; maintain a common requirements-change log for any late changes.\r\n- Same target technology families and security boundaries; document exact dependency versions and where unavoidable differences occur.\r\n- Same external independent acceptance matrix recorded **before** either method\u0027s first implementation commit.\r\n- Keep automated test harness separate from the prompt inputs; do not bias Vibe by injecting a finished SDD specification.\r\n- Preserve Git commit provenance, prompt timestamps (when available), red runs, false test assumptions, screenshots, review decisions, and deployment blockers.\r\n- Use separate environment configuration and namespaced/isolated state; never commit credentials.\r\n\r\n## Student oversight and prompt provenance\r\nEach **Vibe** prompt is drafted for review in ordinary English close to the student\u0027s own voice. Only the actual student\u0027s confirmed final text is sent to an agent, and only that exact executed text receives an execution record. Assistant-authored drafts are labelled as such. SDD AI inputs and outputs are recorded with the real agent identity; never claim interactive Copilot commands were executed unless their logs show that.\r\n\r\n## Assessment and limitations\r\nPASS/FAIL/BLOCKED/NOT TESTED per test per condition, based on actual evidence; a successful build is not acceptance or security proof. Test suites differ only where a method-specific requirement is explicitly noted. Do not add code to frozen versions after comparative testing without recording a new snapshot. Report informed-design bias, order effects, missing active-time measurements, and unverified external OAuth or privacy claims. No causal generalization or guaranteed grade.\r\n\r\n## Workflow order\r\n1. Preserve the approved charter, baseline data and test matrix; freeze a single baseline commit SHA.\r\n2. Create both condition branches **at precisely the same SHA**.\r\n3. Obtain student approval for V-001 before any Vibe coding or execution.\r\n4. Run Vibe prompt-by-prompt, recording prompts, results, corrections and defects.\r\n5. Run official Spec Kit with a supported coding agent on the independent SDD branch, recording actual commands, stages and approvals.\r\n6. Run common black-box tests against frozen snapshots; retain failing outcomes.\r\n7. Assemble the seven-section Moodle experience report from artifacts, noting every missing source.\r\n","Path":"docs/EXPERIMENT_PROTOCOL.md"}
{"Content":"# Nordljud SDD — Master Requirements Brief (MBR-B-002)\r\n**Research condition:** B — Independent Specification-Driven Development with official GitHub Spec Kit  \r\n**Date:** 2026-10-30 (Europe/Helsinki)  \r\n**Status:** **AI_DRAFT — OPTION C POLICY APPROVED; EXACT MASTER TEXT AND EXTENSION NOT YET APPROVED**  \r\n**Student\u0027s verbatim policy approval:** `research/SDD_INPUT_04_OPTION_C_STUDENT_APPROVAL_2026-10-30.md`  \r\n**Implementation:** **NOT STARTED**. No official Spec Kit stage executed. This file is a human-review brief, not a generated `spec.md` or coding instruction.\r\n\r\n## A. Purpose, actors and research boundary\r\nBuild **Nordljud**, a responsive Swedish-through-English learning web application that lets learners study reliable source-linked Swedish vocabulary, see translations and verb forms, practise, use Guest Mode, and optionally authenticate for private progress. Primary actors: Swedish learner/Guest and authenticated learner. Secondary actors: student-researcher, course assessor and authorized test operators. Do not claim linguist certification or measured learning effectiveness.\r\n\r\n**Research comparison:** Condition A is an already frozen, informed, feedback-driven Vibe Coding implementation; Condition B creates an **independent** implementation via the official Spec Kit stages. Compare identical pre-registered CORE F01–F15 outcomes as the **primary** result. Evaluate any later user-requested features as **separately versioned EXTENDED PARITY**, never rewrite the original benchmark or present later features as initial requirements. Report knowledge transfer, chronology, scope asymmetry and missing test evidence as limitations.\r\n\r\n## B. Shared inputs, fixed scope and technology constraints\r\n- Start only from original approved `docs/PROJECT_CHARTER_PC-001.md`, `shared-content/PRODUCT_BRIEF.md`, `shared-content/SOURCE_MANIFEST.md`, the original shared datasets and `evaluation/ACCEPTANCE_MATRIX.md`.\r\n- CEFR levels: **A2, B1, B2, C1**. Each level has **456 semantic/sense records** and **455 distinct written verb spellings**; four levels total **1,824 sense records**. There are **two separate meanings of `sticka`** per level. Maintain distinct sense identity.\r\n- Use the identical, unchanged original `shared-content/verb-library/A2.json`, `B1.json`, `B2.json`, `C1.json` and `mission-seeds.json` identified by `SOURCE_MANIFEST.md`. Preserve stored Swedish/English examples; do not invent missing forms, examples, translations or linguistic certification.\r\n- Original common technology **families**: Next.js, React, TypeScript, Supabase, GitHub, Vercel and browser Swedish speech when supported. Exact dependency versions, interfaces, storage schema, privacy mechanism and layout are choices for **Spec Kit Plan**, subject to these constraints; this brief does not supply Vibe code or architecture.\r\n- Shared explicit exclusions: payment, generative chat tutor, speech-recognition/scoring, admin/social features, large newly authored curriculum and production-grade localization. Android app, PWA push notifications and scheduled push delivery are also excluded from this comparison.\r\n- **Method isolation:** SDD codebase, tests, deployments, Auth and private data must be separate from Vibe. No copying Vibe source, SQL, CSS, tests, screenshots or release-workflow templates; the SDD agent must not inspect the Vibe retrospective and prompt ledger.\r\n\r\n## C. CORE requirements — primary, unchanged F01–F15 acceptance contract\r\nEach ID below states an observable **what/why**; implementation choices belong in the later Plan. The authoritative original F01–F15 wording and its pre-registration date remain unchanged.\r\n\r\n**C01 / F01 — Levels and missions.** Learners can choose each of the four CEFR levels and receive a distinct level-appropriate mission from the frozen source inputs.\r\n\r\n**C02 / F02 — Source-backed examples.** Swedish examples and English translations agree with the frozen source; users can reveal/hide English assis…706 tokens truncated… with real negative cross-account tests; UI concealment alone is insufficient.\r\n\r\n**C13 / F13 — Mobile and keyboard.** The essential study, navigation and login flows work on a narrow viewport and keyboard alone, including visible focus and clear controls. Do not prescribe Vibe\u0027s specific tabs or accordion.\r\n\r\n**C14 / F14 — Sensitive data and failures.** No privileged secret appears in client code or public bundles; real errors produce actionable, non-disclosing feedback and safe retry or Guest fallback where applicable.\r\n\r\n**C15 / F15 — Reproducibility.** Record exact source SHA, dependencies/versions, install, TypeScript/typecheck, tests, build, provider deployment and actual browser acceptance cases. Passing CI, a READY Preview or an OAuth redirect alone is not a live authentication/security PASS.\r\n\r\n## D. Cross-cutting quality and validation rules\r\n- **Data fidelity:** preserve exact immutable teaching data, including incomplete forms and semantic ambiguities; never fill gaps with unsupported AI-generated Swedish.\r\n- **Privacy and security:** least privilege, owner-based backend access checks, no service-role key in client, protected OAuth redirects, minimal synthetic data and redacted evidence. Separate legitimate authorization is required for external provider setup, real test identities and database modifications.\r\n- **Usability:** practical error feedback, readable responsive interaction and accessible essential controls; the later specification and checklist must define measurable scenarios rather than assert untested accessibility certification.\r\n- **Reliability:** tests must include both expected and failure paths, including absent/partial source fields and unavailable cloud/audio/provider functionality; do not mark unavailable live services as PASS.\r\n- **Test fairness:** independently reproduce the original F01–F15 tests for both frozen implementations. Each result is PASS, FAIL, BLOCKED or NOT TESTED with environment, steps, expected/actual, tested SHA and source/screenshot evidence. Do not artificially inflate score based on unit-test counts.\r\n- **Research integrity:** retain actual human/AI roles, approvals, stage artifacts, failures, code changes and timestamps where recorded. Do not invent elapsed development times, cost, security proof or a comparative causal conclusion.\r\n\r\n## E. Option C — separate EXTENDED PARITY scope, secondary evaluation only\r\n**Student APPROVED Option C\u0027s methodology, not yet the exact E01–E07 feature contract.** This section is a **distinct, pending versioned amendment**: `research/SDD_INPUT_05_EXTENDED_PARITY_AMENDMENT_AI_DRAFT_2026-10-30.md`. If explicitly approved, define a second feature specification and independent EXT-AC acceptance suite. Do **not** change, renumber or enlarge primary F01–F15.\r\n\r\n**E01 — Sense-relevant illustrations:** where included, display an appropriately licensed and accurately meaning-matched verb illustration/photo; report actual coverage separately.\r\n\r\n**E02 — Daily micro-lessons:** expose a small, predictable selection of authentic source-backed lessons for a local day without falsely claiming newly authored Swedish materials.\r\n\r\n**E03 — Daily Archive:** permit viewing eligible historical daily selections; never conflate reconstructed past lessons with the user\u0027s attendance.\r\n\r\n**E04 — Completion and Undo:** user explicitly marks or reverses a completion; viewing alone is not completion or language mastery.\r\n\r\n**E05 — Remind Me Later:** a deliberate per-sense review reminder with due/snooze and user removal, distinguishable from favorites and studied flags; no unsolicited push.\r\n\r\n**E06 — 7-/14-day recall:** optional eligible source-grounded review checks with honest scoring, appropriate timing and correct/incorrect feedback.\r\n\r\n**E07 — Extension persistence and privacy:** Guest records follow explicitly disclosed browser boundaries; authenticated extension records are owner-isolated and survive appropriate refresh/re-login.\r\n\r\n**Secondary acceptance:** EXT-AC01–EXT-AC07 track the above one-to-one and are reported **in a separate denominator** from F01–F15. Even a completed extension does not alter the pre-registered primary score. Record the informed, sequential order effect: SDD received a structured extension set after the Vibe condition discovered these features incrementally.\r\n\r\n## F. Matters for genuine Spec Kit Clarify (do not silently decide implementation here)\r\n1. How should level switching behave if a source sense has no reliable counterpart in another level?\r\n2. Exactly which Guest preferences/practice records must persist across a same-browser refresh, and how does a guest become a signed-in user without accidental data mixing?\r\n3. Is email password recovery in CORE acceptance or in a separately tracked refinement? What are supported provider test conditions?\r\n4. Which mission/practice records count as completion and are required to persist for F11?\r\n5. Which independent SDD backend and authorized test identities can safely demonstrate F09–F12 without altering Vibe data?\r\n6. Which real device/browser/audio environments are available for F03/F13, and what accessibility behavior can actually be evidenced?\r\n7. For E01–E07, what feature coverage, retention limits, date/time behavior and test identities are approved? These questions belong to the **secondary amendment** and must not delay an otherwise clarified CORE spec.\r\n\r\n## G. Official Spec Kit process and human checkpoints\r\n- Work only from the original neutral `condition/spec-driven` branch/source baseline. The researcher-only audit and Vibe frozen source are NOT inputs to the coding agent.\r\n- On exact student approval of this English Master, initialize official Spec Kit with a supported coding agent and record **genuine** integration/version and command outputs. Do not pretend Spec Kit has been run just because this brief exists.\r\n- Apply the documented full sequence: **Constitution → Specify → Clarify → Plan → Checklist → Tasks → Analyze → Implement → Converge**, with real review at significant decision points. Constitution is project governance; Specify captures WHAT/WHY; Plan makes independent HOW choices; task implementation requires checked and reviewed quality gates. The exact agent skill syntax depends on its integration.\r\n- **Primary first:** generate and approve CORE specification, plan and acceptance cases before CORE implementation.\r\n- **Secondary separately:** only after a versioned human approval of the E amendment, specify/clarify/plan/tasks/implement its independent additional scope and evaluate EXT-AC without rewriting CORE.\r\n- Do not paste a completed SRS or Vibe solution into a single coding prompt; use genuine Spec Kit artifacts and approvals. Distinguish reviewer-approved quality checklist from tests run against software.\r\n- Record full stage inputs/outputs, exact SHAs and human decisions. Finish with one fixed-SHA SDD research snapshot, comparable primary black-box results, separate secondary comparison if executed, and an evidence-based university report.\r\n\r\n## H. Pending final student approval / hard stop\r\n**THIS IS AI_DRAFT.** The student\u0027s Option C approval authorized drafting this revision, **not its execution**. Do not run official Spec Kit commands, create SDD app/test code, copy Vibe artifacts or change cloud provider configuration until the student reviews and explicitly approves (a) exact English Master **MBR-B-002** and (b) separately versioned extension amendment **EP-B-001** if secondary scope is to be implemented. Preserve original user wording and approved artifact commit SHAs before real agent execution.\r\n","Path":"docs/sdd-input/MBR-B-002_APPROVED_CORE_MASTER.md"}
{"Content":"# Nordljud SDD — Extended Parity Amendment (EP-B-001)\r\n**Date:** 2026-10-30 Europe/Helsinki  \r\n**Status:** **AI_DRAFT — Option C policy approved; exact extension text NOT YET STUDENT-APPROVED**  \r\n**Research home:** `research/sdd-input-audit-2026-10-30` only. This is not in `condition/spec-driven`.  \r\n**Master:** `research/SDD_INPUT_03_MASTER_REQUIREMENTS_BRIEF_AI_DRAFT_2026-10-30.md` version MBR-B-002.  \r\n**Original primary scope:** unchanged `evaluation/ACCEPTANCE_MATRIX.md` F01–F15.\r\n\r\n## Purpose and fairness declaration\r\nThe Vibe Coding condition acquired additional product features from natural student feedback after the initial shared requirements were established. The student approved **Option C**: report original CORE F01–F15 as PRIMARY and compare later optional features independently as EXTENDED PARITY. The fact these extension requirements are known ahead of SDD creates an **order/information advantage** for the SDD condition, which must be explicitly disclosed. Do not call this original preregistered scope.\r\n\r\n## Secondary feature requirements and objective independent test cases\r\n| Feature ID | WHAT / outcome, not Vibe implementation | Independent acceptance case |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| **E01 — Sense-relevant illustration** | If an illustration is shown, it must correctly correspond to the selected verb\u0027s **specific semantic sense**, with provenance/usage permissions documented; unavailable media has a safe fallback. Report counted coverage rather than silently mandating 26 or reproducing Vibe\u0027s assets. | **EXT-AC01:** inspect selected distinct senses incl. the two `sticka` meanings; images, where present, match meaning and rights evidence exists; missing image does not break learning; record number actually covered |\r\n| **E02 — Daily micro-lessons** | Provide a small daily source-backed learning selection distinct from the core fixed representative mission; deterministic and reproducible for a specified local date; no fabricated Swedish sentences. | **EXT-AC02:** for the same local date and level, repeated views show a consistent set of eligible source-linked items; no unknown source record appears |\r\n| **E03 — Daily Archive** | Permit browsing allowed earlier local dates and reconstructing what daily items corresponded to those dates; do not assert the learner visited/completed them. | **EXT-AC03:** pick an eligible earlier date and confirm consistent source-linked selection; future/unsupported date handled clearly; historical view alone does not mark completion |\r\n| **E04 — Completion and Undo** | Enable explicit self-reported daily completion and reversal; viewing alone never implies accomplishment or verified mastery. | **EXT-AC04:** view without action =\u003e unchanged completion; mark =\u003e recorded completion; Undo =\u003e state removed, with correct feedback and no loss of other progress |\r\n| **E05 — Remind Me Later** | Allow learner to place a **specific sense** into a deliberate reminder queue, inspect/update due/snooze and remove it; distinguish queue from Favorites/Studied. No push/notification permission. | **EXT-AC05:** select a sense; add, snooze and remove reminder; verify due state; the two `sticka` meanings stay independent; no implicit notification |\r\n| **E06 — Seven/fourteen-day recall** | Offer eligible source-backed recall prompts with honest right/wrong scoring and a transparent due/eligibility rule. Do not reward reveal as a correct answer. | **EXT-AC06:** under documented controlled-date inputs, check eligibility at 7 and 14 days, questions cite source data, wrong/reveal earns no credit and correct earns only real credit |\r\n| **E07 — Extension state and privacy** | Keep guest extension state within explicitly stated browser boundaries; keep authenticated extension data private to its owner across supported refresh/re-login, without mixing unrelated accounts. | **EXT-AC07:** test guest local persistence and clearing; with two legitimate users, signed-in extension records survive re-login and negative cross-user read/write/delete attempts fail |\r\n\r\n## Comparison and implementation safeguards\r\n- These **seven tests (EXT-AC01 through EXT-AC07) are secondary**; do not rewrite, blend or reweight original F01–F15. Report primary N=15 and secondary N=7 with separate PASS/FAIL/BLOCKED/NOT TESTED counts, evidence links, exact tested SHA and environment. Partial test results must not be counted as full PASS.\r\n- The late-scope SDD feature set should be **specified after CORE** through its own versioned Spec Kit feature path and approved change request. This amendment provides WHAT/WHY and acceptance; new SDD agent independently designs implementation during Plan. Do not supply Vibe screenshots, React code, original test files, dataset quality reports as templates, SQL or release scripts.\r\n- Additional requirements such as more photos, Android native app, push notifications, PWA and automated notification delivery are outside the approved extension; no purchase/rights inference.\r\n- A delayed external service setup, incomplete photo rights, unreachable Google/Auth provider or untestable two-account privacy is **BLOCKED/NOT TESTED**, not a pass.\r\n- The student must approve **this exact EP-B-001 text independently** before the extension becomes required implementation scope. Approval of Option C **alone** is not an extension-feature approval. Master text MBR-B-002 also awaits exact human approval.\r\n","Path":"docs/sdd-input/EP-B-001_APPROVED_SECONDARY_EXTENSION.md"}
